  "evidence": [
    {
      "pages": [
        28,
        29
      ],
      "finding": "The heading/prose identify TMGi, the innovative X4K3 series; both tables preserve TMG и row names and cover exactly 63,100,160,250,400,630,1000,1250,1600,2500. Row values are not changed or reinterpreted."
    },
    {
      "pages": [
        30
      ],
      "finding": "The small drawing caption expressly names X3K3 and X4K3 and range 40–630. Front/end/plan show a sealed corrugated tank, three HV and four LV upper bushings in separate rows, fill tube and channel base. The six admitted small powers lie within that range; no 40 kVA row is created."
    },
    {
      "pages": [
        31
      ],
      "finding": "The large caption expressly names X3K3 and X4K3 and range 1000–2500. Projections show corrugated walls, three lower HV bushings and four taller LV terminals with flat contact plates, and no conservator. All four large table entries fall within that range."
    },
    {
      "pages": [
        32
      ],
      "finding": "A new chapter starts for TMGiN-630 with on-load regulation. Its external drive and control construction are outside the ordinary TMGi interpretation."
    },
    {
      "pages": [
        30,
        31
      ],
      "finding": "Previously independently reviewed small/large geometry and icon definitions already cite these exact pages; their arbitrary-unit outer topology matches the source drawings. Reuse does not require a newly invented geometry or a source-name correction."
    }
  ],
